# Backend Implementation Rules

## Security
- JWT based authentication
- RBAC for admin endpoints
- Current user from SecurityContext
- No insecure direct object access

## Cache
- Read path: cache first, DB fallback
- Update article => clear article detail cache
- List cache can use short TTL
- Do not use Redis as source of truth

## Messaging
- Kafka only for async side effects
- Consumer must consider idempotency
- Message failures cannot break main business transaction

## Search
- Only published articles should be indexed
- Offline/deleted articles must be removed from search visibility
- Provide rebuild-index capability

## Database
- article metadata and content must be stored in separate tables
- keep audit fields on every table
- no direct DO exposure to frontend
